# SQL's `ORDER BY ... DESC`: the body parses as `sort by`, so `DESC` gets its own DS0105 in the same pass; both fixes apply.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | ORDER BY amount DESC
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..36
  PIPELINE@0..35
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    SORT_OP@15..35
      IDENT@15..20 "ORDER"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      IDENT@21..23 "BY"
      WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
      SORT_KEY@24..35
        NAME_REF@24..30
          IDENT@24..30 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
        IDENT@31..35 "DESC"
  WHITESPACE@35..36 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `ORDER BY` is not an operator
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | ORDER BY amount DESC
  |                ^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: sort rows with `sort by`: `sort by amount desc`

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `DESC` is not a sort direction
  --> query:1:32
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | ORDER BY amount DESC
  |                                ^^^^
  |
  = help: keywords are lowercase: write `desc`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | sort by amount desc
which parses without errors
